From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLLatency: no lead before the pipeline has settled

The lead sums the audio error and the picture's alignment, read from the
timestamp the kernel reports on screen. Before the matcher has seen that
timestamp equal the one handed over, nothing says the two share a base:
on one start the kernel's ran a constant 622 ms behind the player's, the
matcher never settled, and the lead read -615 ms for the whole title.
The audio rate trim walked the audio towards it at full slew.

Hand the trim no lead until the pipeline has settled. The per-sample log
still prints what it reads.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLLatency.h
@@ -102,7 +102,11 @@ public:
   //! will fix, and so the part the audio rate has to walk out.
   std::optional<double> Lead() const
   {
-    if (!m_haveLead)
+    // Not before the pipeline has settled: until the frame on screen has been
+    // matched to the one handed over, a timestamp base the kernel and the player
+    // disagree on reads as the picture being frames off, and the trim would walk
+    // the audio towards it.
+    if (!m_haveLead || !m_settled)
       return std::nullopt;
     return m_leadFilt;
   }
